[00:24.72] The dancer slows her frantic pace
[00:26.87] In pain and desperation
[00:29.21] Her aching limbs and downcast face
[00:31.45] Aglow with perspiration
[00:36.28] Stiff as wire, her lungs on fire
[00:38.63] With just the briefest pause
[00:41.39] The flooding through her memory
[00:43.45] The echoes of old applause.
[00:52.26] She limps across the floor
[00:55.91] And closes her bedroom door...
[00:58.02] 
[01:24.68] The writer stare with glassy eyes
[01:26.27] Defies the empty page
[01:28.99] His beard is white, his face is lined
[01:31.01] And streaked with tears of rage
[01:35.80] Thirty years ago, how the words would flow
[01:37.92] With passion and precision
[01:40.69] But now his mind is dark and dulled
[01:42.76] By sickness and indecision
[01:51.82] And he stares out the kitchen door
[01:55.83] Where the sun will rise no more
[01:57.94] 
[02:09.25] Some are born to move the world
[02:12.60] To live their fantasies
[02:16.61] But most of us just dream about
[02:19.85] The things we'd like to be
[02:24.30] Sadder still to watch it die
[02:27.84] Than never to have known it
[02:32.02] For you, the blind who once could see
[02:36.67] The bell tolls for thee
[02:44.61] The bell tolls for
[02:47.28] 
[04:23.03] For you the blind who once could see
[04:28.33] The bell tolls for thee...
[04:35.23] The bell tolls for thee...
